{"verdict":"changes","notes":"In liveRegistry.cancel, a request can be accepted while the run is visible but before attach stores its context; the later attach never honors the pending request, so the run continues despite a successful cancel response. The cancel method also reads lr.cancel after unlocking while attach writes it under the mutex, which is an unsynchronized access. Make the pending-cancel state and cancel-handle invocation atomic. The flow defers only skip cleanup while the live registry entry exists; after actOnSubject returns, the unchanged subject is eligible again and the next createWorktree call removes the cancelled worktree (and a daemon restart's reapOrphanWorktrees removes it too), so the required inspection state is not preserved. Also define terminal-state handling so a cancel accepted after runPhase returns cannot be recorded as built or another stage failure, and fix the advertised `forest cancel \u003crun-id\u003e --reason ...` form: Go's FlagSet stops parsing at the positional run id, so that form currently rejects the reason flag.","reviewer":"verifier","model":"openrouter/openai/gpt-5.6-luna","def_sha":"8531e5c611fd2ed2","run_id":"20260808T103649Z-branch-forest/163-serve-live-run-status-and-cancel","time":"2026-08-08T10:39:29Z"}
